==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-all over the place.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Prepositional phrase===
{{en-PP}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} In [[multiple]] [[direction]]s or locations, often haphazardly; [[everywhere]].
#: {{syn|en|scattershot}}
#: {{ux|en|They started firing '''all over the place'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|In Genoa there are stray cats '''all over the place'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|I've been looking for you '''all over the place'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Ruth Ozeki|title=All Over Creation|publisher=Penguin|isbn=9781440650048|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=garJ9BwysNEC&lpg=PA267&dq=%22all%20over%20the%20place%22&pg=PA267#v=onepage&q=%22all%20over%20the%20place%22&f=false|page=267
|passage=I couldn't believe it. “This is insane! You don't know what you're getting into, Dad. We can't have lots of people swarming '''all over the place'''. You're supposed to be getting rest.”}}
# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} [[inconsistent|Inconsistent]]; lacking a clear [[pattern]]; with a large amount of [[variation]].
#: {{syn|en|at random}}
#: {{ux|en|I asked each person in turn, and their answers were '''all over the place'''.}}
#*{{quote-web|en|date=December 1 2023|author=Emma Sanders|title=England 3-2 Netherlands|work=BBC Sport|url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67577192|passage=England were '''all over the place''' for the majority of the opening 45 minutes as gaps broke in defence.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|everywhere}} {{l|en|all over hell's half acre}}; {{l|en|all over the shop}}; {{l|en|all over the gaff}}; {{l|en|all over the map}}; {{l|en|all over the board}}; {{l|en|here, there and everywhere}}; {{l|en|up hill and down dale}}

